extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 18: Mystic Russia pp.69-71, read from the text layer. IMPORTED UNDER D4, and it is the entry the bestiary reading found most inverted: the heading tags it Non-Player Character & Villain and its Player Note gives it the WARMEST endorsement of the eight Woodland Spirits. NO xp_table, per D3, and THIS IS THE ONLY ONE OF THE SIX THE BOOK GIVES A LADDER FOR: ''player characters (if allowed) start at first level and use the same experience table as the Dragon Hatchling.'' xp_table is a literal array rather than a named reference, all seven Dragon Hatchling classes in this catalog omit it and take DEFAULT_XP_TABLE from xpTableFor() in js/leveling.js, so the book''s own pointer resolves HERE to the default - which is exactly what omitting the key produces. regression.mjs also refuses any R.C.C. that carries one. ITS SKILLS ADVANCE AND THE OTHER FIVE CREATURES'' DO NOT: the book ends this entry''s skill line ''Selected skills increase by level'', where the Domovoi, Leshii, Polevoi, Vodianoi and Spirit Wolf all say the skills do not advance. So the four choice groups carry NO per_level and inherit each catalog row''s own figure, while the two named skills keep per_level 0. TWO OF THIS ENTRY''S NUMBERS ARE FORM-DEPENDENT AND ONLY ONE FORM IS STORED: three attacks per melee as a human and five as a wolf, and every selected skill at -30% in wolf form. bonuses and skill percentages are unconditional by rule - the same reading the Gypsy Beguiler''s animal-form block took in batch 2 - so attacks_base carries the human three and the wolf figures are natural abilities. It is the only one of the six with NO magic and the only one with eight psionic powers. Three of the eight needed the catalog''s own spelling rather than the book''s: Commune with Spirits is Commune with Spirit, Object Read is Object Read (Psychometry), and the book''s Impervious to Poison - on the Polevoi - is Impervious to Poison/Toxin. The text layer carries this book''s digit cipher: the M.D.C. line prints ''P.E.x2 +!D6xlO'' and the life span ''3D6xlO''."
